    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective date: September 23, 2026</p>
    <p>This policy explains how the Auto Clicker Android app handles information. References to "we", "us", and "our" mean the developer of Auto Clicker, who can be contacted at <a href="mailto:gkspacedev@gmail.com">gkspacedev@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    <p><strong>The current app stores automation tasks and run history on your device. It does not upload these records to us or provide cloud synchronization.</strong> If you contact support or open an external website, those interactions are handled separately as explained below.</p>

    <h2>1. Information used on your device</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Tasks and recorded actions:</strong> task names, touch positions or areas, gesture paths, durations, waits, selected apps, and the order of actions. These are used to edit, preview, and execute the flows you configure.</li>
      <li><strong>Run history:</strong> task and action identifiers, result messages, completion or failure status, and timestamps. These help display recent execution results.</li>
      <li><strong>Installed-app information:</strong> Android-provided package names, labels, icons, and package metadata for apps visible to the app picker. This information is used locally to show app choices and configure open-app or wait-for-app actions. Some metadata may be cached on the device.</li>
      <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> theme, language, consent records, onboarding progress, the selected task, and floating-control settings. Some execution and editing state is temporary and is not saved.</li>
      <li><strong>Display information:</strong> screen dimensions and related configuration used to map recorded positions and draw overlays or previews.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This on-device information is not sold, uploaded for advertising, or sent to a developer-operated analytics service by the current app.</p>

    <h2>2. Accessibility Service</h2>
    <p>Recording and executing automation require Android Accessibility Service access. You control this access in Android Settings. Viewing or editing a saved task does not by itself grant that access.</p>
    <p>While the service is enabled, the app receives window-change events, including the foreground app's package and window class information. It uses these events locally to recognize when a selected app or the launcher enters the foreground, including while the Auto Clicker screen is not visible. The current service does not request the ability to retrieve screen text or the view hierarchy.</p>
    <p>The service performs taps, long presses, gestures, and system navigation actions according to the task you configure. During capture, the app records touch input and replays captured actions on the target screen. That replay can operate the other app. The separate in-app trajectory preview uses a simulation canvas.</p>
    <p>Enabling the service is not permission for independent decision-making. Automation follows the sequence and repetition settings you choose. You can stop a run or disable the service in Android Settings. An action already dispatched to another app may finish after Stop is pressed; stopping cannot undo that action.</p>
    <p>The in-app accessibility disclosure and consent are separate from this policy. This policy does not replace the permission explanation shown before enabling accessibility access through the app.</p>

    <h2>3. Information you send to support</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we receive your email address, message, and any attachments or diagnostic information you choose to send. We use them to respond to your request, investigate reported issues, and keep necessary support records. Please avoid sending passwords, payment information, or sensitive screenshots.</p>
    <p>Email is handled by email service providers. They process communications under their own terms and privacy policies. We do not automatically attach your task database or recorded actions to support messages.</p>

    <h2>4. External apps, websites, and sharing</h2>
    <p>Opening Google Play, a community link, a policy page, or an email app takes you to a third-party service. Sharing the app passes the app recommendation text and store link to the destination you choose. Those services handle the information you provide under their own policies.</p>
    <p>Actions replayed in another app may cause that app to process or transmit information, just as manual interactions can. Auto Clicker does not control the other app's data practices. Review the target app and task before running automation.</p>
    <p>When you visit a website hosting this policy, your browser sends information such as your IP address and browser details to its hosting provider to load the page. The supplied policy pages contain no analytics scripts, cookies, or tracking pixels. Hosting and browser services may have their own processing and retention practices.</p>

    <h2>5. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>Saved tasks remain on the device until you delete them or clear the app's data. Deleting a task does not necessarily delete earlier run-history records. Clear Auto Clicker's storage in Android Settings to remove the app's local tasks, history, cached information, preferences, and consent records. Uninstalling normally removes app-private data as well. Files or messages you separately saved or sent outside the app are not removed by these actions.</p>
    <p>The current app does not create an online user account or maintain a remote copy of your task database. We cannot recover local tasks after their deletion. Support correspondence is retained only as needed to address requests, maintain necessary support records, and comply with applicable obligations. Contact us to request deletion of information you sent to support.</p>

    <h2>6. Security</h2>
    <p>Local app data is stored using Android's app-private storage protections. The current app disables standard Android app-data backup. Device security, system software, and third-party services remain outside our control. No storage or communication method can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>

    <h2>7. Your choices and rights</h2>
    <p>You can change or delete tasks, stop automation, disable accessibility access, and clear local app data. Depending on applicable law, you may also have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, object to, or obtain a copy of personal information we hold, or withdraw consent where processing relies on it. To make a request, email <a href="mailto:gkspacedev@gmail.com">gkspacedev@gmail.com</a>. We may need information reasonably necessary to verify and respond to the request. You may also contact the relevant data-protection authority.</p>

    <h2>8. Children</h2>
    <p>Auto Clicker is a general-purpose automation utility and is not designed specifically for children. If you believe a child has sent us personal information through support, contact us so we can review and address it in accordance with applicable law.</p>

    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy when the app or its data practices change. The effective date above identifies the current version. Where required, we will provide notice and obtain consent before introducing materially different processing.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions or requests relating to Auto Clicker, email <a href="mailto:gkspacedev@gmail.com">gkspacedev@gmail.com</a>.</p>
